# Git must not rewrite line endings in this repository.
#
# data/snapshot/manifest.json records the sha256 of every committed CSV, and
# data/verify.py recomputes those hashes as a hard check. Git for Windows
# defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout - the
# file content is unchanged to a human and completely different to sha256, so a
# reviewer cloning on Windows would see "sha256 mismatch - file was edited after
# fetch" on a snapshot nobody touched.
#
# The same applies to llm_cache/ and logs/: the cache is content-addressed and
# the decision log is compared line by line, so neither may be rewritten in
# transit either.

* text=auto eol=lf

data/snapshot/** -text
llm_cache/**     -text
logs/**          -text
